	<item>
		<title>Waterline&#8217;s Penthouse Will Be Ready For You on September 1st</title>
		<link>https://austin.towers.net/waterlines-penthouse-will-be-ready-for-you-on-september-1st/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jude Galligan]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:39:05 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[rainey street district]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[waterline]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://austin.towers.net/?p=94785</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[The Waterline, Austin&#8217;s tallest tower, is finally ready to welcome residents after years of construction. Serving as the gateway to the Rainey District, the Waterline is responsible for much of the Waller Creek Greenway <a href="https://www.austintexas.gov/watershed-protection/projects/confluence">Confluence</a> &#160;build-out in the district. Today, the first MLS listing popped up and it&#8217;s for a 69th floor two-bedroom, priced at &#8211;...]]></description>
		
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Apollo Chooses Austin</title>
		<link>https://austin.towers.net/apollo-chooses-austin-texas/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jude Galligan]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 11:56:33 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://austin.towers.net/?p=94776</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Apollo Global Management ( <a href="https://ticker.id/APO">$APO</a> ) has announced that <a href="https://ticker.id/c/squawk-on-the-street/9am-hour-u-s-japan-yen-intervention-stocks-rally-as-oil-prices-slide-astrazeneca-bristol-myers-m-a-buzz-8-3-26?s=1756970&#38;e=1775712">Austin has been chosen</a> as its innovation and emerging technology hub. Notably, Austin was in the running against Miami, Palm Beach and Nashville. &#160; Reports keep referring to this deal as a &#8220;second headquarters&#8221;; implying that Apollo is not quite ready to abandon its New York City roots, and this isn&#8217;t...]]></description>
		
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Well, That Backfired</title>
		<link>https://austin.towers.net/well-that-backfired/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jude Galligan]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 19 Feb 2026 15:58:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[News]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://austin.towers.net/?p=94765</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[We&#8217;ve all heard cars that backfire incessantly. The siren song of enthusiastic, gifted, drivers who enjoy announcing their car&#8217;s presence at stop lights. A proposed new law is on deck to limit how much exhaust noise a &#8220;person of ordinary sensibilities&#8221; must tolerate. City Council is expected to vote on the <a href="https://services.austintexas.gov/edims/document.cfm?id=467767">ordinance</a> at their next meeting....]]></description>
		
		
		
			</item>
