					<description><![CDATA[The 56-story <a href="https://austin.towers.net/meet-the-modern-austin-condo-tower-headed-for-the-modern-rainey-district/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Modern Austin Residences</a> condo tower project celebrated its official &#8220;topping out&#8221; this week, with the building now reaching its maximum structural height of 658 feet at the northeast corner of Davis and Rainey Streets on the north end of the <a href="https://austin.towers.net/tag/rainey-street-district/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rainey Street District</a> in downtown Austin. It&#8217;s just one of multiple tower projects currently redefining the <a href="https://austin.towers.net/rainey-streets-future-skyline-looks-like-a-second-downtown-austin/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">skyline of this neighborhood,</a> which already contains...]]></description>
		
